# Toolcrib

> An AI-generated, AI-optimized React UI toolkit — a structural component/theme/event-bus system that gets vendored directly into a consumer's project (`toolcrib init`, full-vendoring like shadcn, not an npm dependency), designed specifically to stop AI-driven UI generation from re-inventing inconsistent Tailwind soup on every turn.

Toolcrib ships {{componentCount}} production components across five categories ({{categoryList}}), plus a {{eventChannelCount}}-channel typed event bus for cross-tree communication instead of prop-drilling, an HSV-derived CSS-variable theme system with a four-layer override hierarchy, and a Zod-schema-driven form engine — documented for AI consumption via generated, source-derived docs that can't silently drift from what's actually in the code.

